# Configuration for the Python server (server/main.py).
#
# The native macOS app does not need this file. The app has no configuration
# file and no environment variables. This file applies only to the legacy
# FastAPI server in server/.
#
# Copy this file to .env and give it to uvicorn, which reads it with
# python-dotenv:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#     ./.venv/bin/uvicorn server.main:app --env-file .env --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
#
# You can also export the variables yourself. Nothing reads .env automatically.
# Each value below is a default that already works. .env only replaces them.
# This project contains no secrets, no accounts and no API keys.

# The WhisperKit model to load at startup.
#
# Read finding 1 in docs/FINDINGS.md before you change this value. The `_turbo`
# suffix of WhisperKit marks a compute variant. It is NOT the large-v3-turbo
# model of OpenAI. OpenAI publishes that model under its date stamp,
# `large-v3-v20240930`. A match on the name "large-v3-turbo" gives you a
# different model that is much slower.
#
# server/models.py holds the catalogue of ids that this variable accepts.
ASR_MODEL=openai_whisper-large-v3-v20240930_turbo

# The maximum number of concurrent live transcription sessions. The server
# refuses a session above this limit with an `at_capacity` error. It does not
# put the session in a queue.
#
# One session already uses most of one model instance, thus the useful limit is
# low. Finding 7 in docs/FINDINGS.md gives the measured degradation. Partial
# latency holds to 4 streams, but the number of commits per stream falls by
# approximately one third.
ASR_MAX_SESSIONS=3
